1","name":"CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT 1: Increasing funding to school districts","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Minnesota Constitution be amended to increase the funding going to all school districts from the permanent school fund, which is a fund that supports school districts without raising individual income or property taxes, effective July 1, 2027?"},{"id":"mn-carver-sd2859-school-district-question-1-isd-2859","name":"SCHOOL DISTRICT QUESTION 1 (ISD #2859): Revoking Existing Referendum Revenue Authorization^  Approving New Authorization","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"The school board of Independent School District No. 2859 (Glencoe-Silver Lake Public Schools) has proposed to revoke the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization of $601.98 per pupil and to replace that authorization with a new authorization of $1,445 per pupil. The proposed referendum revenue authorization would be applicable for ten years commencing with taxes payable in 2027, and increase each year by the rate of inflation beginning with taxes payable in 2028, unless otherwise revoked or reduced as provided by law.\n\nShall the school districts existing referendum revenue authorization be revoked, and the increase in the revenue proposed by the school board of Independent School District No. 2859 be approved?","schoolNum":"2859","area":"Glencoe-Silver Lake"}]}